{"module":"media","voice":"male","duration":166.6,"segments":[{"el":"title","text":"Media and image-making","start":0.0,"end":2.1,"words":[[0.05,0.62],[0.62,0.9],[0.9,1.95]]},{"el":"intro","text":"How people are shown shapes how they're treated, including who a caller sees as “suspicious.”","start":2.9,"end":8.09,"words":[[2.94,3.15],[3.15,3.5],[3.5,3.57],[3.57,3.85],[3.85,4.2],[4.2,4.41],[4.41,4.69],[4.69,5.18],[5.43,5.99],[5.99,6.13],[6.13,6.27],[6.27,6.55],[6.55,6.76],[6.76,6.9],[6.9,7.53]]},{"el":"h0","text":"Minstrelsy and “Jim Crow”","start":8.44,"end":10.55,"words":[[8.48,9.4],[9.4,9.67],[9.67,10.04],[10.04,10.41]]},{"el":"s0","text":"In the 1830s white performer Thomas D.","start":11.25,"end":14.16,"words":[[11.3,11.45],[11.45,11.6],[11.6,12.33],[12.33,12.62],[12.62,13.06],[13.06,13.42],[13.42,13.64]]},{"el":"s0","text":"Rice blacked up to play a character he called “Jim Crow,” and minstrel shows became America's most popular entertainment for decades.","start":14.51,"end":23.82,"words":[[14.56,14.89],[14.89,15.3],[15.3,15.47],[15.47,15.63],[15.63,15.96],[15.96,16.13],[16.13,16.71],[16.71,16.88],[16.88,17.21],[17.21,17.54],[17.54,17.95],[17.95,18.2],[18.2,18.86],[18.86,19.2],[19.2,19.69],[19.69,20.36],[20.36,20.77],[20.77,21.35],[21.35,22.34],[22.34,22.51],[22.51,23.17]]},{"el":"s0","text":"The character's name later became the name for the whole system of segregation laws.","start":24.17,"end":29.79,"words":[[24.21,24.37],[24.37,25.01],[25.01,25.33],[25.33,25.74],[25.74,26.22],[26.22,26.38],[26.38,26.7],[26.7,26.86],[26.86,27.02],[27.02,27.34],[27.34,27.83],[27.83,27.99],[27.99,28.87],[28.87,29.19]]},{"el":"s0","text":"Caricatures sold products for more than a century; the Aunt Jemima brand was only retired in 2020–2021.","start":30.14,"end":38.82,"words":[[30.19,31.0],[31.0,31.37],[31.37,31.96],[31.96,32.11],[32.11,32.26],[32.26,32.48],[32.48,32.63],[32.63,33.29],[33.55,33.7],[33.7,33.92],[33.92,34.44],[34.44,34.81],[34.81,35.03],[35.03,35.4],[35.4,35.92],[35.92,36.07],[36.07,38.29]]},{"el":"h1","text":"The Birth of a Nation","start":39.72,"end":40.95,"words":[[39.76,39.89],[39.89,40.09],[40.09,40.23],[40.23,40.36],[40.36,40.76]]},{"el":"s1","text":"D.W.","start":41.65,"end":42.51,"words":[[41.7,42.15]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Griffith's 1915 film portrayed Reconstruction's Black officeholders as menacing and the Ku Klux Klan as heroes.","start":42.86,"end":51.12,"words":[[42.9,43.46],[43.46,44.5],[44.5,44.82],[44.82,45.38],[45.38,46.51],[46.51,46.83],[46.83,47.71],[47.71,47.87],[47.87,48.43],[48.43,48.67],[48.67,48.83],[48.83,48.99],[48.99,49.39],[49.39,49.71],[49.71,49.87],[49.87,50.51]]},{"el":"s1","text":"It was screened at the White House.","start":51.47,"end":53.65,"words":[[51.52,51.65],[51.65,51.85],[51.85,52.25],[52.25,52.38],[52.38,52.51],[52.51,52.78],[52.78,53.11]]},{"el":"s1","text":"The NAACP protested it nationwide.","start":54.0,"end":57.47,"words":[[54.05,54.2],[54.2,55.22],[55.22,55.92],[55.92,56.07],[56.07,56.93]]},{"el":"s1","text":"That November, a new Ku Klux Klan was founded at Stone Mountain, Georgia, and grew to millions of members in the 1920s.","start":57.82,"end":66.88,"words":[[57.87,58.09],[58.09,58.77],[59.03,59.18],[59.18,59.4],[59.4,59.55],[59.55,59.93],[59.93,60.23],[60.23,60.45],[60.45,60.97],[60.97,61.12],[61.12,61.5],[61.5,62.1],[62.36,62.88],[63.14,63.37],[63.37,63.59],[63.59,63.74],[63.74,64.27],[64.27,64.42],[64.42,64.86],[64.86,65.01],[65.01,65.16],[65.16,66.29]]},{"el":"h2","text":"Crime news","start":67.78,"end":68.97,"words":[[67.81,68.35],[68.35,68.79]]},{"el":"s2","text":"The 1968 Kerner Commission, appointed after urban uprisings, criticized news organizations for reporting “from the standpoint of a white man's world.”","start":69.67,"end":80.58,"words":[[69.72,69.88],[69.88,71.19],[71.19,71.5],[71.5,72.12],[72.39,73.01],[73.01,73.32],[73.32,73.63],[73.63,74.41],[74.68,75.45],[75.45,75.76],[75.76,76.77],[76.77,76.92],[76.92,77.46],[77.46,77.77],[77.77,77.93],[77.93,78.7],[78.7,78.86],[78.86,79.01],[79.01,79.32],[79.32,79.63],[79.63,80.02]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Studies of local TV news have found Black people shown as criminal suspects more often than arrest data would predict.","start":80.93,"end":88.52,"words":[[80.95,81.41],[81.41,81.57],[81.57,82.03],[82.03,82.34],[82.34,82.64],[82.64,82.87],[82.87,83.26],[83.26,83.56],[83.56,83.95],[83.95,84.25],[84.25,84.41],[84.41,85.02],[85.02,85.63],[85.63,85.79],[85.79,86.09],[86.09,86.32],[86.32,86.71],[86.71,87.09],[87.09,87.32],[87.32,87.93]]},{"el":"s2","text":"In 1989 five Black and Latino teenagers were convicted in the Central Park jogger case after intense coverage and a full-page newspaper ad calling for the death penalty; they were exonerated in 2002.","start":88.87,"end":103.75,"words":[[88.91,89.07],[89.07,90.3],[90.3,90.62],[90.62,90.95],[90.95,91.19],[91.19,91.77],[91.77,92.5],[92.5,92.66],[92.66,93.4],[93.4,93.56],[93.56,93.73],[93.73,94.3],[94.3,94.54],[94.54,94.95],[94.95,95.28],[95.28,95.61],[95.61,96.1],[96.1,96.75],[96.75,97.0],[97.0,97.16],[97.16,97.81],[97.81,98.55],[98.55,98.71],[98.71,99.12],[99.12,99.28],[99.28,99.45],[99.45,99.69],[99.69,100.35],[100.63,100.88],[100.88,101.04],[101.04,102.02],[102.02,102.18],[102.18,103.16]]},{"el":"s2","text":"In 1995 political scientist John DiIulio warned of coming juvenile “superpredators”; the wave never came, and he later expressed regret.","start":104.1,"end":114.46,"words":[[104.15,104.3],[104.3,105.56],[105.56,106.23],[106.23,106.9],[106.9,107.2],[107.2,108.02],[108.02,108.32],[108.32,108.47],[108.47,108.84],[108.84,109.51],[109.51,110.48],[110.74,110.89],[110.89,111.18],[111.18,111.48],[111.48,111.85],[112.11,112.34],[112.34,112.49],[112.49,112.86],[112.86,113.45],[113.45,113.97]]},{"el":"h3","text":"How much does coverage change minds?","start":115.36,"end":118.0,"words":[[115.4,115.59],[115.59,115.85],[115.85,116.05],[116.05,116.57],[116.57,117.02],[117.02,117.48]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Experiments have found that viewers shown a Black suspect in a news story become more supportive of punitive policies than viewers shown a white suspect or none.","start":118.7,"end":128.25,"words":[[118.76,119.68],[119.68,119.9],[119.9,120.29],[120.29,120.51],[120.51,120.89],[120.89,121.2],[121.2,121.35],[121.35,121.66],[121.66,122.19],[122.19,122.34],[122.34,122.49],[122.49,122.8],[122.8,123.18],[123.18,123.56],[123.56,123.71],[123.71,124.24],[124.24,124.4],[124.4,125.0],[125.0,125.54],[125.54,125.77],[125.77,126.15],[126.15,126.45],[126.45,126.6],[126.6,126.91],[126.91,127.44],[127.44,127.52],[127.52,127.82]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Researchers debate how large and lasting these effects are outside the lab.","start":128.6,"end":133.07,"words":[[128.64,129.22],[129.22,129.65],[129.65,129.87],[129.87,130.16],[130.16,130.38],[130.38,130.81],[130.81,131.03],[131.03,131.47],[131.47,131.54],[131.54,132.05],[132.05,132.19],[132.19,132.48]]},{"el":"h4","text":"Cameras that turned the story","start":133.97,"end":135.99,"words":[[134.01,134.54],[134.54,134.8],[134.8,135.15],[135.15,135.33],[135.33,135.77]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Ida B. Wells used reporting to expose lynching.","start":136.69,"end":140.75,"words":[[136.74,137.05],[137.05,137.28],[137.67,137.99],[137.99,138.3],[138.3,138.85],[138.85,139.0],[139.0,139.55],[139.55,140.18]]},{"el":"s4","text":"In 1955 Mamie Till-Mobley insisted on an open casket for her son Emmett, and Jet published the photographs.","start":141.1,"end":149.46,"words":[[141.15,141.31],[141.31,142.59],[142.59,142.99],[142.99,143.63],[143.63,144.27],[144.27,144.43],[144.43,144.59],[144.59,144.99],[144.99,145.47],[145.47,145.63],[145.63,145.79],[145.79,146.02],[146.02,146.42],[146.7,146.94],[146.94,147.26],[147.26,147.82],[147.82,147.98],[147.98,148.86]]},{"el":"s4","text":"In 2020, 17-year-old Darnella Frazier recorded George Floyd's murder; she received a special Pulitzer citation in 2021.","start":149.81,"end":159.41,"words":[[149.86,150.0],[150.0,150.93],[151.18,152.32],[152.32,152.75],[152.75,153.32],[153.32,153.82],[153.82,154.18],[154.18,154.61],[154.61,154.97],[155.22,155.36],[155.36,155.79],[155.79,155.93],[155.93,156.36],[156.36,156.93],[156.93,157.57],[157.57,157.72],[157.72,158.86]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Many of the 911 calls that led to CAREN laws became known because someone recorded them.","start":159.76,"end":165.74,"words":[[159.82,160.1],[160.1,160.24],[160.24,160.37],[160.37,161.69],[161.69,161.96],[161.96,162.17],[162.17,162.38],[162.38,162.52],[162.52,162.86],[162.86,163.07],[163.07,163.48],[163.48,163.76],[163.76,164.11],[164.11,164.52],[164.52,165.01],[165.01,165.28]]}]}